A||||3||Matt85_GT||battery, alt, drain???||||5||
Z||000000||Matt85_GT||06-04-2000||03:47 PM||||Here is the problem. I charged up my battery for the summer and have been driving the car for a couple weeks. Then went to lunch after driving to work, it started fine then when I started to pull into the restaurant the radio started blinking off and on. I shut the car off went and ate then came back out and the starter just clicked.  I got it jump started and drove home.  The next morning the car started fine, and also started after work.  But it seemed to be low on electrical power, windows slow and tach jumped when turn signal went on. Then after about five miles the windows had more power and went up and down a lot faster.  I am wondering what the problem is Battery, alternator, or a slow drain somewhere.  I checked all the battery connections and they were tight.  If it is a slow drain what are some of the most probable to check.  Thanks in advance, Matt 85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||bad88||06-04-2000||06:04 PM||||first thing to check is the easy stuff<BR>does the battery have 12 volts with engine off<BR>with engine on does battery voltage increase? (alt. charging)<BR>turn on accessories like radio, lights etc and see how the power is affected then.  That will at least narrow down the search to the right circuit||||reg||3
Z||000002||Mark||06-04-2000||10:11 PM||||Could be as simple as a battery going bad.  Have it load tested.  Also, make sure all your connections are CLEAN and tight (i.e., battery cables, ground braids, etc.).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||06-04-2000||10:12 PM||||Could be as simple as a battery going bad.  Have it load tested.  Most parts stores will do this for free.  Also, make sure all your connections are CLEAN and tight (i.e., battery cables, ground braids, etc.).||||reg||1
